<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23177" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-fervesco</span></b> , ferbŭi, 3,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
			n.</i>, <i>to boil down</i>, <i>to
			boil</i>, <i>to grow hot</i>, <i>be
				heated</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fabae tertia pars ut infervescat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 90</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulsum quod inferbuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					2, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hoc ubi inferbuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 4, 67</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne infervescat aqua sole,</span>”
				<i>be heated</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 12, 60, § 183</span></i>
			.— <b>Poet.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solem infervescere fronti arcet,</span>”
				<i>to burn on the forehead</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					13, 341</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
